WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.980
<b>Rare Anime World</b>

00:00.650 --> 00:02.750
<i>This time on </i>Rare Anime World<i>,</i>

00:02.750 --> 00:06.300
<i>we'll be looking at an anime from 40 years 
ago that was only broadcast in Saitama</i>

00:06.300 --> 00:08.310
<i>called </i>Mysterious Mikorin<i>.</i>

00:08.310 --> 00:09.740
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:09.740 --> 00:11.740
<i>Hey, all you small fry!</i>

00:10.740 --> 00:11.740
What is this?

00:12.080 --> 00:13.990
<i>This is the mermaid VTuber,</i>

00:14.620 --> 00:17.390
Himeuo Yorumun!

00:14.820 --> 00:15.240
<b>Popular VTuber Himeuo Yorumun Announces Her Retirement</b>

00:22.590 --> 00:27.380
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

00:22.590 --> 00:27.380
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

01:48.000 --> 01:50.510
<b>Takamagahara Hospital</b>

01:48.620 --> 01:53.880
<b>A Live Performance, a Curse, and the Person Inside</b>

01:48.620 --> 01:53.880
<b>A Live Performance, a Curse, and the Person Inside</b>

01:50.510 --> 01:52.510
<b>Are These Crimes Being Committed
by a Hacker Who Page-Jacked Popular
\hVTuber Himeuo Yorumun's Official Site?</b>

01:51.020 --> 01:54.010
The uproar is escalating rapidly.

01:54.410 --> 01:58.760
Yorumun is taking over popular 
streamers' videos one after another.

01:58.760 --> 02:01.070
It just doesn't add up.

02:01.070 --> 02:02.500
It's ominous.

02:05.020 --> 02:08.730
It doesn't make sense for the damage 
to start spreading indiscriminately

02:08.730 --> 02:10.030
instead of among her fans.

02:10.030 --> 02:11.780
<b>Ametsuchi Nodoka</b>

02:11.780 --> 02:13.280
Get out!

02:13.280 --> 02:15.680
Please calm down, Nodoka.

02:15.680 --> 02:17.030
What does it matter?

02:17.700 --> 02:21.180
I'm simply worried about your health.

02:21.180 --> 02:25.040
Let me do what I like, too! Just a little!

02:27.590 --> 02:30.100
Is Nodoka-chan's room around here?

02:30.100 --> 02:31.340
Yes, it's over there.

02:31.340 --> 02:33.050
Get out already!

02:33.420 --> 02:34.550
Nodoka...

02:34.550 --> 02:36.760
Just get out!

02:47.820 --> 02:48.970
Nodoka?

02:50.060 --> 02:51.290
Occhan.

02:51.290 --> 02:53.900
Sorry to drop in without notice.

02:54.410 --> 02:58.460
Um, this is my older brother Ren, 
and that's the apartment wife.

02:58.460 --> 02:59.330
Huh?

02:59.640 --> 03:05.330
Oh, are you Wakazukuri-senpai's 
older sister? It's nice to meet you.

03:05.330 --> 03:07.730
U-Um, Nodoka?

03:07.730 --> 03:14.490
Sorry. I have to make up for lost time, 
so I can't talk right now.

03:21.510 --> 03:22.840
This is it.

03:24.040 --> 03:25.350
Ren-nii?

03:25.350 --> 03:27.350
What are you doing? Wait!

03:27.710 --> 03:31.030
What do you think you're doing 
to your little sister's friend?

03:31.030 --> 03:34.360
I almost had it, too. 
So much for the element of surprise.

03:34.360 --> 03:36.780
The explanation comes first. So explain.

03:37.400 --> 03:41.310
Nodoka-chan, you've heard the news 
about people falling unconscious, right?

03:41.310 --> 03:45.880
Himeuo Yorumun isn't who you think she is.

03:46.870 --> 03:51.260
The current Yorumun is a Curiosity that 
has broken free from her digital image.

03:51.260 --> 03:56.380
There have long been similar stories of 
Curiosities that escaped from paintings.

03:56.700 --> 03:59.550
One such story is 
"The Horse From the Painting,"

04:00.100 --> 04:05.530
a folktale about a horse escaping from an 
ema tablet and spoiling the fields each night.

04:06.270 --> 04:09.900
They say that, once reins and a post 
were drawn onto the ema,

04:10.230 --> 04:12.650
the Curiosity ceased its actions immediately.

04:12.650 --> 04:17.980
So you were trying to draw something 
onto Yorumun to overwrite her data?

04:17.980 --> 04:20.910
Regrettably, I lack the finesse for that.

04:21.330 --> 04:24.180
Besides which, rather than 
cutting off the source entirely,

04:24.180 --> 04:27.160
my objective here is simply 
to save Oto's friend.

04:27.590 --> 04:29.270
Kuji goshin hou:

04:28.290 --> 04:35.460
<b>Kuji Goshin Hou
(Nine-Character Self-Defense)</b>

04:29.640 --> 04:33.960
a method of self-defense said to have its origins in the classic Chinese text <i>Baopuzi</i>,

04:33.960 --> 04:36.690
practiced in Shugendo and Onmyodo.

04:37.490 --> 04:42.680
The grid of lines created by the nine characters 
in the phrase is known as a kuji-mon.

04:39.460 --> 04:42.680
<b>\hKuji-Mon\h
(Nine-Character Device)</b>

04:42.680 --> 04:48.810
Even now, some ama divers wear the sigil 
when they dive to ward off misfortune.

04:49.500 --> 04:51.820
It's a simplistic solution,

04:51.820 --> 04:57.900
but drawing the device directly on her tablet 
should be enough to block Yorumun.

04:59.220 --> 05:00.860
We want to save you.

05:00.860 --> 05:02.700
Please let me see your tablet.

05:02.700 --> 05:03.700
No!

05:03.700 --> 05:06.200
Father told you to do this, didn't he?

05:06.200 --> 05:10.110
Yorumun only ever tries 
to encourage her fans!

05:10.110 --> 05:12.210
She hasn't done anything wrong!

05:12.210 --> 05:15.740
But she's the reason you collapsed, isn't she?

05:15.740 --> 05:16.710
No!

05:20.470 --> 05:22.470
Just get out!

05:22.470 --> 05:23.720
Go away!

05:24.660 --> 05:27.410
But, Nodoka...

05:29.480 --> 05:31.140
Ametsuchi-san?

05:31.140 --> 05:32.610
Uname-sensei?

05:33.310 --> 05:34.860
Why are you here?

05:34.860 --> 05:37.980
There's someone I want you to meet.

05:38.930 --> 05:41.680
The rest of you are here 
at just the right time, too.

05:41.680 --> 05:43.630
Someone you wanted her to meet?

05:43.630 --> 05:44.490
Mikamo-chan?

05:45.870 --> 05:48.070
Th-Thank you for having me.

05:48.950 --> 05:50.000
That voice...

05:50.330 --> 05:51.660
Yorumun?

05:53.070 --> 05:54.940
You must be Nodoka-san, right?

05:54.940 --> 05:59.510
As well as Oto-san, her older brother, 
and Sumireko-san.

05:59.510 --> 06:00.400
Right?

06:00.400 --> 06:01.620
Yes.

06:01.620 --> 06:05.510
When Uname-chan told me everything 
that happened, I knew I had to see you.

06:05.510 --> 06:06.660
Huh?

06:07.940 --> 06:11.130
Please save Yorumun!

06:14.070 --> 06:16.400
Let me introduce you more properly.

06:16.700 --> 06:19.230
This is Hanamura Mikamo-chan.

06:18.440 --> 06:21.150
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:18.730 --> 06:21.150
<b>Hanamura Mikamo</b>

06:19.570 --> 06:25.460
I got to know her while I was hospitalized, 
as she'd been coming in for regular checkups,

06:25.460 --> 06:27.210
and we became good friends.

06:27.660 --> 06:33.540
I asked her about her work, but at the time, 
I didn't know what a "VTuber" was.

06:35.530 --> 06:37.670
What's wrong, Mikamo-chan?

06:39.650 --> 06:40.420
What?

06:40.420 --> 06:42.970
"Her boobs are so big they scare me"?

06:42.970 --> 06:44.430
Really?

06:44.780 --> 06:47.870
It's all right. They aren't scary boobs.

06:47.870 --> 06:48.680
Hey.

06:50.270 --> 06:56.440
Uname-chan told me you were the 
breast person to ask about Curiosities.

07:00.590 --> 07:01.440
What?

07:01.440 --> 07:04.110
"Seriously, her boobs scare me"?

07:04.110 --> 07:06.740
Don't worry. They're just lumps of fat.

07:06.740 --> 07:10.450
Uname-sensei, most of what you're 
saying is pretty mean, you know?

07:11.090 --> 07:14.590
She's like a totally different person 
compared to when she's streaming.

07:14.590 --> 07:16.960
The exact opposite of her 
cheerful, energetic persona.

07:17.910 --> 07:19.210
I...

07:19.640 --> 07:22.340
I'm completely different 
from my streams, aren't I?

07:22.870 --> 07:25.970
But when I was little, I was an active child.

07:26.430 --> 07:30.470
I was twice as energetic as anyone else, 
and I always wanted to stand out.

07:30.880 --> 07:33.630
I even thought that 
I might want to be an idol.

07:35.080 --> 07:36.720
But in fifth and sixth grade,

07:37.350 --> 07:40.460
I started having difficulty 
keeping up in gym class.

07:40.460 --> 07:42.680
Gradually, I began to lose endurance.

07:45.740 --> 07:49.990
I was diagnosed with a incurable progressive 
disease when I was twelve years old.

07:50.820 --> 07:52.980
I lost the ability to walk.

07:53.740 --> 07:55.870
The most difficult thing for me was that

07:55.870 --> 07:59.880
whenever I did anything, 
someone else had to take care of me.

08:00.540 --> 08:03.870
Whether it was climbing 
stairs, going shopping,

08:03.870 --> 08:05.530
or even using the bathroom,

08:05.530 --> 08:08.260
I always put others through a lot of trouble.

08:08.840 --> 08:11.750
"I'm sorry I couldn't give you a healthy body."

08:11.750 --> 08:13.350
My mom said that all the time.

08:14.490 --> 08:17.270
When I saw the way my parents 
had to take care of me,

08:17.270 --> 08:20.830
the emotional stress of it 
made me want to run away.

08:22.690 --> 08:25.320
I couldn't find any hope in my life.

08:26.650 --> 08:31.530
It was Himeuo Yorumun 
who saved me from all that.

08:32.480 --> 08:35.410
As a VTuber, I didn't need to show my face,

08:35.410 --> 08:37.280
<b></b>New Member Application

08:35.410 --> 08:37.280
<b></b>Agency Exclusive VTuber Audition

08:35.980 --> 08:38.540
and I could act with just my upper body.

08:38.910 --> 08:43.040
It was a long shot, but I went ahead 
and sent in an application.

08:44.040 --> 08:50.300
When I did, the higher-ups, managers, 
modelers, and designers all empathized with me.

08:50.300 --> 08:53.840
They all worked fervently 
to create a character for me.

08:55.390 --> 08:59.720
Out of consideration for my body, 
they made her a mermaid.

09:00.290 --> 09:03.890
Her name came from other words for 
mermaids and from legends of the sea.

09:10.410 --> 09:15.330
I cheered on people like me, struggling 
in situations they had no control over.

09:16.080 --> 09:18.770
I'd only ever been on the receiving 
end of people's support,

09:18.770 --> 09:20.940
but now I could make others happy, too!

09:23.120 --> 09:26.930
But my body couldn't endure it.

09:28.080 --> 09:31.970
I'd gotten so caught up in the joy 
of being helpful to others

09:28.380 --> 09:36.850
<b>Popular VTuber Himeuo Yorumun Announces Her Retirement</b>

09:31.970 --> 09:36.240
that I pushed myself too hard 
too many times and ruined everything.

09:38.240 --> 09:41.770
When I learned of the incidents, 
I wanted to do something,

09:41.770 --> 09:46.240
but I didn't have any idea how 
to deal with something so unreal.

09:47.230 --> 09:51.340
Uname-chan told me that 
you two might understand.

09:52.240 --> 09:56.960
Please! Help me stop Yorumun!

09:57.790 --> 10:02.460
You haven't run into any streams 
hijacked by Yorumun yourself, have you?

10:02.810 --> 10:07.960
No, not even once. 
She won't appear in front of me.

10:08.940 --> 10:10.170
I see.

10:10.510 --> 10:13.170
We're changing objectives.

10:13.730 --> 10:15.490
Let's save Yorumun.

10:16.020 --> 10:19.770
You sure were quick to agree 
to Mikamo-san's request.

10:20.080 --> 10:24.770
No need to be jealous. You're the 
only one for me, Sumireko-san.

10:24.770 --> 10:27.840
Save the sleeptalk for when you're 
actually asleep, Adashino-kun.

10:27.840 --> 10:30.780
More importantly, is it even possible?

10:31.110 --> 10:33.000
Can we save Yorumun?

10:33.660 --> 10:36.780
If she were a regular tsukumogami, 
it would likely be impossible.

10:36.780 --> 10:39.530
Are you saying she isn't?

10:39.930 --> 10:42.390
There are different types of tsukumogami.

10:42.390 --> 10:43.820
There are?

10:43.820 --> 10:49.920
Normally, a tsukumogami's enmity is directed 
toward the creator or user who discarded it.

10:49.920 --> 10:54.680
And yet, she hasn't appeared to 
Mikamo-san, but to her viewers.

10:55.130 --> 10:58.970
And when Yorumun does appear, 
all she does is cheer people on.

10:59.630 --> 11:03.490
It's likely that Yorumun's 
objective isn't revenge.

11:04.160 --> 11:06.700
She's a garei you created.

11:04.720 --> 11:08.190
<b>\hGarei\h
(Image Spirit)</b>

11:06.700 --> 11:07.770
"Garei"?

11:09.090 --> 11:13.570
A Curiosity depicted in an anthology 
from the Bunsei era, <i>Ochiguri Monogatari</i>.

11:14.190 --> 11:16.320
One day, at a temple called Kajuu-ji,

11:15.230 --> 11:21.150
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

11:15.520 --> 11:20.530
<b>Kajuu-ji</b>

11:16.320 --> 11:20.280
a woman began appearing from a painting 
on a worn-out folding screen.

11:20.800 --> 11:22.930
When they investigated, 
they learned that the screen

11:22.930 --> 11:25.620
was painted by a distinguished 
artist and thus was precious.

11:25.620 --> 11:28.480
They repaired the painting 
and stored the screen carefully,

11:28.480 --> 11:30.710
and the woman never appeared again.

11:31.140 --> 11:32.880
Which means that garei are born

11:32.880 --> 11:36.760
of images like paintings and carvings 
that people have poured their hearts into.

11:36.760 --> 11:39.720
They're Curiosities driven by the 
sentiment their artist instilled in them.

11:40.390 --> 11:43.220
It's likely that Yorumun is a type of garei.

11:43.720 --> 11:46.990
She's trying her hardest to 
fulfill your wish, isn't she?

11:47.660 --> 11:49.210
My wish?

11:49.660 --> 11:51.980
To cheer everyone on.

11:52.470 --> 11:54.480
You said it yourself, didn't you?

11:54.480 --> 11:59.340
It's not normal for this many people to 
collapse just from being cheered for, though.

11:59.340 --> 12:02.490
She must be desperate to fulfill her duty.

12:03.130 --> 12:08.250
Day and night, the Curiosity whispers 
endless encouragements in people's ears.

12:08.810 --> 12:12.000
The people she supports keep 
working until they collapse.

12:13.170 --> 12:16.110
Excessive support isn't 
so different from a curse.

12:18.140 --> 12:21.760
This is, so to speak, a sort 
of artificial divine possession.

12:22.070 --> 12:26.770
There is a method called kamiage that 
can be used to send the spirit away.

12:27.070 --> 12:31.410
However, forcing a Curiosity that 
cheers people on to stop doing that

12:31.770 --> 12:34.980
would mean turning Yorumun back 
into no more than a simple image.

12:34.980 --> 12:35.780
What?

12:36.400 --> 12:38.780
To do that, we'll need your help, Mikamo-san,

12:39.350 --> 12:41.530
and the help of her fans.

12:41.990 --> 12:44.150
I won't help you!

12:44.500 --> 12:47.020
I won't erase Yorumun.

12:47.360 --> 12:51.790
If you stop her, that means 
she'll disappear, right?

12:52.140 --> 12:54.540
I don't want that!

12:54.540 --> 12:58.050
This Yorumun won't disappear like you did!

12:58.050 --> 13:00.710
She won't abandon her fans!

13:02.050 --> 13:05.810
Yorumun and the person inside her 
are two different people!

13:07.770 --> 13:08.440
Nodoka-san...

13:08.440 --> 13:10.810
Don't speak to me with that voice!

13:12.440 --> 13:15.830
I won't be around for much longer.

13:17.070 --> 13:20.330
Soon, I won't be able to talk 
or go out like this anymore.

13:21.250 --> 13:23.820
But I'm glad I did what I did.

13:24.490 --> 13:28.330
Thanks to Yorumun, my dream 
of becoming an idol came true.

13:28.950 --> 13:34.460
My only regret is that people are saying 
bad things about Yorumun because of me.

13:35.650 --> 13:37.960
It's the one thing I can't leave behind.

13:38.400 --> 13:42.710
That's why I have to do something 
about it while I can still move!

13:48.540 --> 13:50.410
What do I have to do?

13:51.240 --> 13:53.070
Please gather her fans together.

13:53.480 --> 13:55.050
An empty livestream would be fine.

13:55.540 --> 13:59.330
We're going to prepare a stage for Yorumun.

13:59.940 --> 14:02.570
<b>Himeuo Yorumun</b>

14:02.570 --> 14:06.320
<b>Announcement</b>

14:06.320 --> 14:08.580
<b>Please spread the word!
Yorumun will be holding a live graduation concert!</b>

14:19.410 --> 14:23.510
And instantly, there are twenty 
thousand people waiting for the stream.

14:23.510 --> 14:25.800
The only ones here are her fans.

14:25.800 --> 14:27.640
The preparations are complete.

14:28.180 --> 14:31.640
What specifically does this kamiage entail?

14:31.640 --> 14:37.900
Deities and spirits are firstly greeted, 
secondly made welcome, and thirdly seen off.

14:37.900 --> 14:41.580
That's the most basic format 
of Japan's festivals.

14:42.700 --> 14:46.470
Unseen spirits are made to 
manifest through divine possession.

14:46.470 --> 14:51.910
The necessary ingredients for that are a focus
for the possession, a priestess, and believers.

14:52.220 --> 14:55.840
Here, that would be the avatar, 
the actor, and the fans.

14:56.190 --> 15:00.800
VTubers just happen to fulfill all those 
requirements in a simulated manner on the net.

15:01.210 --> 15:04.880
Which is why we can follow the steps by 
making her feel welcome, then seeing her off.

15:05.270 --> 15:07.800
Basically, we're going to 
gently persuade her to go.

15:08.140 --> 15:10.930
And not just anyone's words will reach her.

15:11.340 --> 15:13.580
It has to be the voice of the priestess.

15:15.440 --> 15:19.570
The biggest problem is whether 
Yorumun will come or not.

15:19.570 --> 15:21.440
Yorumun will be here, no matter what!

15:21.440 --> 15:24.450
She's always watching her fans!

15:25.950 --> 15:29.020
What's this? Everyone's having so much fun.

15:29.020 --> 15:31.450
Are you having a festival without telling me?

15:34.680 --> 15:38.710
Let me play, too! I'm gonna 
give it everything I've got!

15:39.710 --> 15:41.820
Mikamo-san, hurry! The salutation!

15:41.820 --> 15:43.210
R-Right!

15:43.210 --> 15:44.720
Nodoka!

15:45.790 --> 15:47.790
You want to save your little sister?

15:47.790 --> 15:50.220
How admirable! I'm rooting for you!

15:50.220 --> 15:51.720
<i>This is bad!</i>

15:51.720 --> 15:53.190
Ren-nii!

15:51.720 --> 15:53.190
Adashino-kun!

15:55.280 --> 15:58.130
Adashino-san! Sumireko-san!

16:25.230 --> 16:27.260
Are we... safe?

16:27.470 --> 16:29.260
Hot! That's hot!

16:29.260 --> 16:32.760
It's so hot! I don't get it, 
but that was awful!

16:33.300 --> 16:35.220
That's the Chinrinki for you.

16:35.220 --> 16:37.270
It's a level above your average Curiosity.

16:37.270 --> 16:41.020
Um, what was I trying to do again?

16:41.020 --> 16:43.270
Huh? I forgot.

16:43.600 --> 16:48.030
It was looking bad, but we got lucky. 
She seems like she might listen right now.

16:52.030 --> 16:54.370
Let's begin her graduation concert.

16:55.790 --> 16:57.540
<b>Himeuo Yorumun            Nice to meet you, Yorumun.</b>

16:58.880 --> 17:00.140
Is that me?

17:01.030 --> 17:04.720
The person inside? Could it be 
you're the person inside me?

17:03.170 --> 17:05.040
<b>IroMegane          The person inside?!!</b>

17:04.720 --> 17:06.190
Wow! This is amazing!

17:05.040 --> 17:05.790
<b>IroMegane          The person inside?!!</b>

17:05.050 --> 17:05.790
<b>Wakuyama Daikin          Then who is this Yorumun?</b>

17:05.790 --> 17:06.790
<b>IroMegane          The person inside?!!</b>

17:05.790 --> 17:06.790
<b>Wakuyama Daikin          Then who is this Yorumun?</b>

17:05.800 --> 17:06.790
<b>Torasu Bicycles               There is no person inside</b>

17:06.190 --> 17:09.050
I always wanted to talk to you like this!

17:06.790 --> 17:07.790
<b>IroMegane          The person inside?!!</b>

17:06.790 --> 17:07.790
<b>Wakuyama Daikin          Then who is this Yorumun?</b>

17:06.790 --> 17:07.790
<b>Torasu Bicycles               There is no person inside</b>

17:06.800 --> 17:07.790
<b>Haruka            What's going on?</b>

17:07.790 --> 17:08.540
<b>Wakuyama Daikin          Then who is this Yorumun?</b>

17:07.790 --> 17:08.540
<b>Torasu Bicycles               There is no person inside</b>

17:07.790 --> 17:08.540
<b>Haruka            What's going on?</b>

17:07.800 --> 17:08.540
<b>Hashishi             What's happening here?</b>

17:08.540 --> 17:09.040
<b>Torasu Bicycles               There is no person inside</b>

17:08.540 --> 17:09.040
<b>Haruka            What's going on?</b>

17:08.540 --> 17:09.040
<b>Hashishi             What's happening here?</b>

17:08.550 --> 17:09.050
<b>Ranburetta           Someone please explain.</b>

17:09.320 --> 17:13.550
Oh, oh! Have you been watching me? 
I've been working so hard!

17:13.550 --> 17:16.060
I'm cheering everyone on!

17:16.960 --> 17:21.100
I'm so happy! I never imagined 
I'd get to talk to my person inside!

17:22.020 --> 17:24.060
<b>Himeuo Yorumun                I could say the same thing.</b>

17:22.020 --> 17:24.060
I could say the same thing.

17:24.560 --> 17:27.900
I never imagined the day would come 
that you'd be able to talk with me.

17:24.560 --> 17:30.070
<b>Himeuo Yorumun              I never imagined the day
would come that you'd be able to talk with me.</b>

17:28.600 --> 17:30.070
I know, right?

17:31.820 --> 17:35.200
<b>Himeuo Yorumun             Hey, Yorumun.
I'd like you to take a look at this news link.</b>

17:31.820 --> 17:35.200
Hey, Yorumun. I'd like you to 
take a look at this news link.

17:35.730 --> 17:38.050
News? What is it?

17:46.240 --> 17:49.590
I'm... causing problems for people?

17:49.590 --> 17:51.720
No! That isn't it!

17:54.770 --> 17:58.900
<i>The one who supported me when 
I was depressed about work was you!</i>

17:58.900 --> 18:02.570
<i>The reason I was able to hang in there when 
I was hospitalized was your livestreams!</i>

18:02.570 --> 18:05.820
<i>You give me the motivation to work 
hard every morning. Thank you.</i>

18:05.820 --> 18:09.860
<i>Thanks to your livestreams, 
I was able to forget the bad things in life.</i>

18:11.280 --> 18:16.880
<i>Thank you, Yorumun. Because of you, 
we can each walk on our own now.</i>

18:20.140 --> 18:22.570
I see. Yes.

18:33.840 --> 18:37.920
I... We did our very best, didn't we?

18:37.920 --> 18:39.290
Yes, we did.

18:39.290 --> 18:43.280
Thank you. Everyone will be all right now.

18:43.280 --> 18:44.610
Really?

18:44.610 --> 18:46.550
Yes, really.

18:46.550 --> 18:48.580
I see. I see!

18:48.890 --> 18:52.390
And I'll be joining you soon.

18:54.350 --> 18:55.810
No, you won't.

18:55.810 --> 18:56.520
Huh?

18:56.520 --> 18:59.910
You still have so many 
good things ahead of you!

19:20.560 --> 19:27.730
<i>No matter where you are,</i>

19:27.730 --> 19:33.550
<i>I'm yelling my support for you</i>

19:34.180 --> 19:40.160
<i>Smile and catch your dream</i>

19:40.660 --> 19:46.490
<i>Grab it and go beyond it</i>

20:11.600 --> 20:12.720
Yorumun!

20:12.720 --> 20:13.780
Mikamo-san?

20:14.230 --> 20:16.010
Your legs... Are they...

20:19.310 --> 20:20.530
Yorumun!

20:36.340 --> 20:37.800
Yorumun!

20:55.020 --> 20:58.820
Another name for Himeuo is "Jinja-hime."

20:59.320 --> 21:04.370
Jinja-hime is a mermaid roughly 
six meters long with two horns.

21:02.360 --> 21:06.580
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

21:02.650 --> 21:06.580
<b>Jinja-hime</b>

21:04.880 --> 21:09.100
She is a Curiosity who is said to both 
foretell epidemics and dispel diseases.

21:09.440 --> 21:11.510
So she's sort of like an amabie?

21:11.510 --> 21:13.010
Exactly.

21:13.010 --> 21:16.420
And her ability to ward off disease

21:16.420 --> 21:19.090
is strengthened according to 
the number of images of her.

21:20.230 --> 21:24.100
That means the reason Yorumun 
hijacked so many other streams...

21:24.100 --> 21:26.600
Yes. She was quite impressive.

21:26.920 --> 21:29.600
She spread herself far and wide 
through her own efforts,

21:29.980 --> 21:31.870
all for the person she wanted to save.

21:36.060 --> 21:38.610
The one Yorumun most wanted to encourage

21:38.610 --> 21:41.440
was you, Mikamo-san.

21:43.870 --> 21:49.070
Yorumun, who once was your dream, 
saved your spirit.

23:34.980 --> 23:39.980
<b>Cats, Swimsuits, and a Black Aeonium</b>

23:36.120 --> 23:40.440
Next time, "Cats, Swimsuits, 
and a Black Aeonium."
